<%- include("partials/public-shell-start", { pageTitle }) %>

<section class="legal-page">
  <div class="legal-hero">
    <span class="legal-hero__badge">Election Portal Rules</span>
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p>
      These Terms of Use explain the rules for using
      <strong><%= settings.electionName %></strong> for voting, nominations,
      observer access, and election administration.
    </p>
    <small>Last updated: July 4, 2026</small>
  </div>

  <div class="legal-layout">
    <aside class="legal-summary-card legal-summary-card--terms">
      <h2>Important Rules</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use only your own staff ID, phone number, OTP, and application number.</li>
        <li>One eligible staff member is allowed one completed vote.</li>
        <li>Do not share admin, observer, or voter access credentials.</li>
        <li>Do not attempt to manipulate, attack, or bypass the system.</li>
        <li>Election committee decisions and official settings control portal access.</li>
      </ul>
    </aside>

    <article class="legal-document">
      <section>
        <h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
        <p>
          By using this portal, you agree to follow these terms, the election
          committee's instructions, and any official rules issued for the election.
          If you do not agree, do not use the portal and contact the committee
          for assistance.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. Eligible Users</h2>
        <p>
          The portal is intended for registered staff voters, approved nomination
          applicants, accredited observers, and authorized administrators. Access
          may be refused or removed if a user is not eligible or misuses the
          system.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. Voter Responsibilities</h2>
        <p>
          Voters must enter accurate staff ID and phone information, keep OTP
          codes confidential, review selections before final submission, and
          understand that a submitted vote cannot be changed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. Nomination Responsibilities</h2>
        <p>
          Nomination applicants must provide truthful information, upload suitable
          photos, submit before the deadline, and keep their application number
          safe for status checks. The committee may approve, reject, or request
          corrections based on the election rules.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. Prohibited Activities</h2>
        <p>
          Users must not submit false information, impersonate another person,
          share private codes, attempt multiple votes, interfere with the portal,
          upload harmful files, bypass CAPTCHA or OTP controls, or attempt
          unauthorized access to admin or observer pages.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. Admin and Observer Use</h2>
        <p>
          Administrators and observers must use their access only for official
          election duties. They must protect login credentials, avoid unauthorized
          disclosure of records, and report suspicious activity immediately.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>7. Election Timing and Availability</h2>
        <p>
          Voting and nomination access may open or close automatically based on
          the dates set by the committee. The portal may be temporarily unavailable
          because of maintenance, internet issues, hosting issues, security checks,
          or other operational reasons.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>8. Results and Records</h2>
        <p>
          Results shown in the portal are generated from submitted records. The
          election committee may review audit logs, archived results, and reports
          before making any official final declaration.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>9. Changes to These Terms</h2>
        <p>
          These terms may be updated when the system, election rules, or security
          requirements change. Continued use of the portal after changes means
          you accept the updated terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>10. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For questions about these terms, contact
          <a href="mailto:jacksmeg99@gmail.com">jacksmeg99@gmail.com</a>
          or call <a href="tel:+233592934612">0592934612</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="legal-note">
        These terms support the transparent operation of the election portal and
        do not replace any official constitution, policy, or election committee
        rule of the organization.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<%- include("partials/public-shell-end") %>
